WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Real humanoid experiments are shown side by side: VLA-50 on the left, VLA-80 in the center, and HOIST on the right. Each robot faces a suspended gray box above a wooden platform with an outlined target.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:15.000
The robots reach toward the suspended boxes as the loads descend. The method names remain visible below each panel.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:23.000
The robots guide the lowering boxes with their hands. Their arm motions and the loads' positions relative to the outlined targets differ across the three panels.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:30.000
The boxes reach the platforms, showing each method's placement. On-screen text identifies these recordings as fully autonomous at one-times speed. Quantitative results are reported separately in the webpage's results tables.
